{
	"set": "zuiddrecht",
	"$comment": "pipelinq's part of the Zuiddrecht example set: the cast's residents and businesses as clients, the businesses' contact people, and the work of KCC employee daan: a phone question from Henk with the call itself, a question from Sanne about her Woo request, a complaint from Fatima, and a lead for CloudGemeente B.V. with Mark as contact. The lead goes into the default pipeline 'Sales' that pipelinq ships. contactsUid is each cast member's own contactsUid; it names no Contacts card until a later pipelinq:contacts:sync writes one with that uid. appConfig makes the cast's KCC group the CRM group and the BRP group, so daan works as an agent; crm_read_group lets dossiq's case handlers (dossiq-medewerkers) read the parties, contact moments and indicators their cases show, with no CRM write right; remove puts the old values back. Install with `occ openregister:example-set:install zuiddrecht` (openregister PR #4603); pipelinq's own `pipelinq:demo:seed` is separate and unchanged. The appointment samples (PqAfspraak, PqAfspraken, PqInloop) add a Locatiebezoek service, Sanne's confirmed site visit two days ahead, handled by daan, and four walk-in customers today.",
	"appConfig": [
		{
			"key": "crm_group",
			"value": "{{cast:kcc.gid}}"
		},
		{
			"key": "crm_read_group",
			"value": "dossiq-medewerkers"
		},
		{
			"key": "brp.allowed_groups",
			"value": "{{cast:kcc.gid}}"
		}
	],
	"objects": [
